  "query_preview": "..\nIssued at 319 AM EDT Fri Oct 2 2026\n\nA good soaking across the area with the rain band that has been\nslowly but steadily working its way through the area from the\nnorthwest to the southeast. Many locations have already seen\nnear to slightly above the 1 inch rainfall mark. Here at the\noffice by 2 AM around 1.28 inches of rainfall had fallen so far.\nThe front will continue to provide light to moderate rainfall\nacross the area and move southeastward bringing rainfall to an\nend over the northwestern portions of the CWA later this morning\nand march southeastward into the afternoon. Cooler temperatures\nwill also arrive behind the boundary and highs today will only\nreach the mid to upper 60s. This cooler and drier trend will \ncontinue through the weekend into next week. Highs will\ngenerally run in the mid to upper 60s with Sunday a brief and\nslight warmup with some locations especially south and east\ngetting into the lower 70s. Lows will also be cool with lows\ngenerally in the 40s but Tuesday morning looks to dip into the\nmid to upper 30s. Will have to watch carefully in the coming\ndays with a shot of clearing which will maximize the \nradiational cooling and perhaps some localized frost may be \npossible especially for the far northern and northeastern \nlocations. However with the still pretty warm ground temps would\nthink this may be averted. Will keep an eye on that \ndevelopment.",
